  "hypothesis_held": true,
  "conclusion": "Detected at: renamed_required_column -> ingest, price_as_text_with_symbols -> clean, dropped_optional_table -> not detected. 2 of 2 scored faults detected; the clean baseline passed: True. 0 mappings were applied without a person. 0 conditions lost rows silently (cleaning reported success while the row accounting did not balance). Detection rate is reported against the baseline on purpose: a detector that flagged everything would otherwise score perfectly.",
  "limitations": [
    "`register_version` returns early on an identical checksum, before it validates anything. That is correct idempotence, but it means a file whose bytes were registered before a contract existed for its dataset is never re-validated. This experiment sidesteps it by registering each condition under a fresh dataset name; a deployment would need a re-validation pass when a contract is introduced or changed. Not a defect, but not covered either.",
    "Only profile and clean are run, so what the feature stage does with a missing optional table - the 'disables its features' half of the hypothesis - is not measured here."
  ],
